119 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 58 0 R
/T (Electronic mail remains one of the most widely used communication channels in both personal and professional environments. Unfortunately, it is also one of the most exploited vectors for cyber-attacks. Phishing is a form of social engineering in which an attacker masquerades as a trustworthy entity and sends fraudulent emails designed to steal sensitive information such as passwords, banking credentials, credit-card numbers, or personal identification data. According to industry threat reports, phishing continues to account for the majority of reported data breaches worldwide, causing enormous financial and reputational damage to individuals and organisations alike.)
/E (Electronic mail remains one of the most widely used communication channels in both personal and professional environments. Unfortunately, it is also one of the most exploited vectors for cyber-attacks. Phishing is a form of social engineering in which an attacker masquerades as a trustworthy entity and sends fraudulent emails designed to steal sensitive information such as passwords, banking credentials, credit-card numbers, or personal identification data. According to industry threat reports, phishing continues to account for the majority of reported data breaches worldwide, causing enormous financial and reputational damage to individuals and organisations alike.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
120 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 58 0 R
/T (The proposed project, AI-Based Phishing Email Detection System, is a full-stack web application developed in the domain of Cyber Security and Natural Language Processing \(NLP\). The application analyses the textual content of an email and classifies it as either legitimate or phishing. Unlike conventional detection tools that rely on a single technique, this system employs a Hybrid Detection Engine that combines a Machine Learning text-classification model with a Rule-Based Heuristic system. The machine learning component provides a data-driven probability score, while the heuristic component scans the text for known phishing indicators such as urgency words, suspicious Uniform Resource Locators \(URLs\), and requests for account credentials. Every heuristic flag artificially boosts the phishing probability, ensuring that obvious phishing attempts are caught even when the statistical model is uncertain.)
/E (The proposed project, AI-Based Phishing Email Detection System, is a full-stack web application developed in the domain of Cyber Security and Natural Language Processing \(NLP\). The application analyses the textual content of an email and classifies it as either legitimate or phishing. Unlike conventional detection tools that rely on a single technique, this system employs a Hybrid Detection Engine that combines a Machine Learning text-classification model with a Rule-Based Heuristic system. The machine learning component provides a data-driven probability score, while the heuristic component scans the text for known phishing indicators such as urgency words, suspicious Uniform Resource Locators \(URLs\), and requests for account credentials. Every heuristic flag artificially boosts the phishing probability, ensuring that obvious phishing attempts are caught even when the statistical model is uncertain.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
121 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 58 0 R
/T <>
/E <>
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
122 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 58 0 R
/T (The project also integrates Optical Character Recognition \(OCR\) technology. Users may paste raw email text directly into the application, or alternatively upload or paste a screenshot of an email \(for example, a screen capture received over a messaging application\). The frontend performs client-side image preprocessing: it computes the average brightness of the image, and if a dark-mode screenshot is detected, the colours are automatically inverted and the contrast is boosted before OCR is applied, which considerably improves text-extraction accuracy. This multi-modal input capability makes the tool practical for real-world scenarios where the original email text is not directly available.)
/E (The project also integrates Optical Character Recognition \(OCR\) technology. Users may paste raw email text directly into the application, or alternatively upload or paste a screenshot of an email \(for example, a screen capture received over a messaging application\). The frontend performs client-side image preprocessing: it computes the average brightness of the image, and if a dark-mode screenshot is detected, the colours are automatically inverted and the contrast is boosted before OCR is applied, which considerably improves text-extraction accuracy. This multi-modal input capability makes the tool practical for real-world scenarios where the original email text is not directly available.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
