/Title (Electronic mail remains one of the most widely used communication channels in both personal and professional environments. Unfortunately, it is also one of the most exploited vectors for cyber-attacks. Phishing is a form of social engineering in which an attacker masquerades as a trustworthy entity and sends fraudulent emails designed to steal sensitive information such as passwords, banking credentials, credit-card numbers, or personal identification data. According to industry threat reports, phishing continues to account for the majority of reported data breaches worldwide, causing enormous financial and reputational damage to individuals and organisations alike.)
