490 0 obj
<<
/Title (The proposed project, AI-Based Phishing Email Detection System, is a full-stack web application developed in the domain of Cyber Security and Natural Language Processing \(NLP\). The application analyses the textual content of an email and classifies it as either legitimate or phishing. Unlike conventional detection tools that rely on a single technique, this system employs a Hybrid Detection Engine that combines a Machine Learning text-classification model with a Rule-Based Heuristic system. The machine learning component provides a data-driven probability score, while the heuristic component scans the text for known phishing indicators such as urgency words, suspicious Uniform Resource Locators \(URLs\), and requests for account credentials. Every heuristic flag artificially boosts the phishing probability, ensuring that obvious phishing attempts are caught even when the statistical model is uncertain.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 311 0 R
/Prev 397 0 R
/Next 588 0 R
>>
endobj
491 0 obj
<<
/Title (The project also integrates Optical Character Recognition \(OCR\) technology. Users may paste raw email text directly into the application, or alternatively upload or paste a screenshot of an email \(for example, a screen capture received over a messaging application\). The frontend performs client-side image preprocessing: it computes the average brightness of the image, and if a dark-mode screenshot is detected, the colours are automatically inverted and the contrast is boosted before OCR is applied, which considerably improves text-extraction accuracy. This multi-modal input capability makes the tool practical for real-world scenarios where the original email text is not directly available.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 311 0 R
/Prev 588 0 R
/Next 398 0 R
>>
endobj
